                        text "edgevar (src/env.rs:294-363) is the largest allocation source: rule bindings are deep-cloned per lookup (env.rs:348-349 clones the whole EvalString including every part), every literal part is cloned into a parts Vec (env.rs:315) then copied again by merge, $in/$out expansion clones a BString per node via nodepath (graph.rs:494-497) then copies through pathlist, and the cycle-guard allocates Vec<String> plus name.to_owned() per level (env.rs:356). Rewrite evaluation to append into one caller-owned byte buffer, holding &EvalString and &BStr references against &Graph instead of returning owned values — the clones are borrow-appeasement, not the samurai design (both C tools evaluate into an owned buffer). nodepath should return &BStr; shell-escaped paths append directly. Replace the recursion-guard stack with a small fixed-capacity buffer of borrowed names (depth in real manifests is 2-4). This is the main lever on the manifest-command-evaluation gap (36.9 ms ronin vs 9.7 ms C samurai in benchmarks/baseline-2026-07-29.md)."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id ronin-edge-metadata-cache
                title "Evaluate each edge's control bindings once and memoize"
                deps (ronin-eval-scratch-buffers)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-30T08:10:11.398169252Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "CommandSpec::evaluate (src/build/command.rs:42-83) runs the full edgevar machinery ten times per edge (command, description, rspfile, rspfile_content, deps, depfile, msvc_deps_prefix, restat, generator, pool), the depfile scan repeats deps and depfile per edge (build.rs:700-705), parseedge evaluates pool and dyndep per edge (parse.rs:280-287), and deps_entry_is_live re-evaluates deps per live log entry during recompaction (deps.rs:668-673). Resolve the fixed control-binding set in one pass per edge sharing one scratch buffer and one resolution stack, memoize the result per edge, and make all consumers read the cached metadata. Boolean bindings (restat, generator, deps presence) should short-circuit on non-empty-binding existence without materializing values."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id ronin-name-interning
                title "Intern binding and rule names as integer symbols"
                deps (ronin-alloc-metrics)
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-30T08:10:19.408401317Z
                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @note
                        text "All binding and rule lookups are String-keyed BTreeMaps: Environment.bindings/.rules and Rule.bindings (src/env.rs:46-56), Edge.bindings (src/graph.rs:67) — byte-wise string comparisons through pointer-chasing tree nodes, with a key allocation per insert. Intern names into a u32 symbol id at scan time (the scanner already yields &str borrowed from the source); binding tables become sorted Vec<(VarId, value)> — most hold 0-3 entries so linear scan over 8-byte pairs beats any tree and empty tables cost nothing. Reserve constant ids for in/in_newline/out so the special-var dispatch in edgevar_inner (env.rs:329-334) becomes an integer compare. Rule tables per environment get the same treatment."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id ronin-phony-console-ids
